h music or encouraging people  in the wrong sorts of pleasures with  music again something that we're going  to see Plato himself talking about in  the mouths of Socrates in the Republic  in a different dialogue right now he  brings the two together finally by  saying you know the art of Medicine one  of the things that were able to do with  it is allow people to enjoy the  pleasures of the table there they're  allowed to enjoy a certain amount of  unhealthy eating because you balance it  out with healthy things and you use the  art of medicine to make sure they're not  going to really do damage to themselves  he says the art of music can do  something quite similar the person who's  actually skilled in music can let us  enjoy a bit of the stuff that's a little  bit risky a little bit going too far  if we just listen to that all the time  it would screw us up they understand the  right amount of proportion for that  there's a certain order that should be  imposed that's what he's saying the art  of music does so the art of music works  with love just as much as medicine does  as a matter of fact they work almost in  parallel or in tandem with each other
 

